  "conversation": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "user": "I need the wall ready for finishing quickly. How does block installation compare with cast-in-situ curing?",
      "assistant": "When your priority is speed, pre-cast hemp-lime blocks generally get the wall ready for finishing much faster than cast-in-situ methods. Because pre-cast blocks arrive already cured, you lay them with lime mortar and can typically begin plaster sequencing after a reference planning window of about 2 to 3 days. \n\nIn contrast, cast-in-situ material is tamped wet into formwork; while forms can often come off the next day, the damp hemp-lime core requires a natural curing window of about 3 to 6 weeks depending on site conditions before you can apply final breathable finishes. Note that exact pricing, current inventory availability, and structural engineering approvals are live operational details not established by these planning figures.\n\nWould you like to calculate the planning wall volume for your specific project dimensions to compare material needs?",
      "stopReason": "completed",
